 day for the pair we walked because we  were really sad that day it was a very  sad day for us both number four this  seems to be a theme when filming intense  television throughout the entirety of  season 3 millie bobby brown lost her  voice due to all the screaming she had  to do during scenes with daker  montgomery in an interview with gma news  she opens up about the predicament i  lost my voice five times  five different times throughout the  eight months of filming i have to go  back into the avr room and start  screaming number five hilarious and  awkward improv a major season three  moment happens in the hawkins  supermarket when mike tries to tell 11  that he loves her most of this scene was  improvised the duffer brothers gave finn  wolfhard a lot of freedom in this  endearing monologue millie bobby brown's  reaction was totally genuine she was  mostly just trying not to laugh because  of how awkward finn was being  like i've never felt like this you know  with anyone before number six  not only for millie bobby brown most of  the cast had their first kiss on the set  of stranger things after looking back on  the scene finn was probably more  embarrassed than millie on this one  this was definitely a notable moment for  the pair and it's gotten a lot easier  since their first time locking lips and  the duffer saw that they're like perfect  he doesn't know how to kiss that's great  number seven speaking of million finn's  first kiss did you know that finn  wolfhard cued her in for it the snowball  dance was home to a couple of iconic  first kisses but sadie sink and caleb  mclaughlin's kiss took about 10 takes  while million finns only took two  there was a lot of pressure on the kids  as tons of people had eyes on them even  giving them awkward high fives and  rounds of applause after it was done to  temper this awkwardness finn told millie  very quietly without moving his lips too  much he was like okay i'm coming in  right as he was about to lean in number  eight yes we're talking about farts  millie bobby brown wasn't the one doing  it but she did have to endure a bus that  was hot boxed with one of her co-stars  farts the duffer brothers shared the  experience in an article for  entertainment weekly millie was getting  more and more frustrated with her male  co-stars case in point we're shooting a  scene in an abandoned bus and one of the  boys decides to fart more than once it  became so toxic in the bus that the crew  had to temporarily evacuate  number nine we still don't know where it  came from as far as we know millie bobby  brown is always professional even from  the young age of 11 but throughout all  these years of filming she was still a  kid and sometimes kids show up to set  covered in glitter the duffer brothers  talked twin pr about the mysterious  glitter that delayed shooting for almost  an hour one day she showed up on set and  she was just covered head to toe in  glitter and she's like i don't know  where this glitter came from number 10 a  little embarrassing a little gross  millie doesn't typically shy away from  difficult scenes or stunts but we did  find out she's not so keen on being  strapped into a harness for a difficult  season 3 scene she was stuck spinning  around in the upside down due to the  fact that she was doing her own stunt  work that day the fear and discomfort on  her face were 100 real i was just  constantly going upside down which kind  of sucked i threw up after number 11.  speaking of dizzy one of millie bobby  brown's most difficult scenes to shoot  in season 3 had her upside down and  screaming at the top of her lungs she  talks about it in an interview with  entertainment weekly i'd say the hardest  thing for me to do is when the monster  grabs my leg because i was lifted up  into the air and i have to scream upside  down which was definitely a lot  being held upside down screaming in  front of all of your friends while  trying to stay in character kind of a  funny moment to imagine  number 12. also known as 11's signature  hairstyle one thing millie bobby brown  learned from playing 11 was how to be  kind and care for others mostly because  of how much hate she endured simply  because of her haircut in an interview  with w magazine she talks about her  struggles with the public after shaving  her head people would laugh at me  without knowing whether i was or wasn't  sick it was hurtful remember the times  where i would like walk on the street  and everybody just sort of freak with  the no hair number 13. typically a great  meal for any occasion we all remember  eleven's introduction she sneaks into  benny's restaurant and steals some fries  from the kitchen eventually he ends up  cooking her a burger in order to ask her  a few questions apparently that scene  was one of millie's least favorites to  shoot at the time because all of the  food was cold naturally she talked to  bon appetit about this unfortunate  culinary experience i had to stuff my  face with cold fries they were so greasy  i had like three burgers and i'd put  them in my mouth and they were cold i  was like are you kidding me she had a  cup beside her and after she would  mutter her line  11  she would spit the burger into a cup and  come back up number 14 not that anyone's  counting one of the most awkward  curveballs that millie had to manage  when starting out on stranger things was  learning how to act without lines i'll  give this back  and you can have as much as you want all  right maybe even some ice cream but you  got to answer a few my questions first  all right at first she definitely felt a  bit self-conscious just utilizing her  facial expressions to convey her  character's emotions  but she obviously did get the hang of it  later on number 15 this definitely makes  for an awkward crying scene in this  unforgettable season 1 episode mike  lucas and dustin ask 11 to lead them to  will they end up following some  emergency vehicles to a quarry where 